    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. For q-74575, cot²θ=csc²θ−1 gives cscθ+1 on the original expression's domain. For q-65446, (cscθ−cotθ)(cscθ+cotθ)=1 gives cotθ. For q-134155, the centered products sum to 8, so population covariance is 8/4=2. For q-134170, the means are 2 and 0 and the centered products sum to −20, so population covariance is −5. For both graph questions, Image #4 is increasing through (0,0), with endpoints (−1,−π/2) and (1,π/2). The arcsine domain is [−1,1], admitting −7/10 and −4/5 in their respective questions; its range is [−π/2,π/2], admitting π/5, and its minimum point is (−1,−π/2). For each three-point question, only point II satisfies x=sin(y) with y in the principal arcsine range. Exponential growth dominates powers, giving limits −1 and 0 for q-75723 and q-75727. Logarithmic growth is slower than linear growth, giving 0 for q-49727, and slower than square-root growth, making q-123703 diverge to positive infinity. These judgments use captured worked solutions, not inferred answer keys or uncaptured grades.",
